  "text": "With reference to Figure 1, calculate the three-firm concentration ratio for\nbranded coffee shop chains.",
  "ms": "Knowledge 1, Application 2, Analysis 2\nThree-firm concentration ratio is the sum of the largest\nmarket share of the biggest three firms as a proportion\nof the whole market (1)\nCalculations e.g.\n• 2681+1025+648 = 4354 (1)\n• 50+40+30+3748 = 3868 (1)\n• 8222 (1)\n• 4354/8222 (1) = 0.53\nAnswer = 52.96%\nAward 5 marks for correct answer (52.96)\nN.B. allow 52-53 or 0.53:1 (5)\n(5)\nN.B. Maximum of 4 marks if no correct answer\ngiven e.g. 0.53 (4)",
