  "section": "B",
  "text": "Nigeria is considering joining the African Continental Free Trade Agreement.\nAssess policies the Nigerian government could use in response to the concerns of\nthe country’s ‘manufacturers and trade unions’ (Extract B paragraph 3) if they join\nthis trading bloc.",
  "ms": "Knowledge 2, Application 2, Analysis 2,\nPossible policies might include e.g.:\n• Supply-side policies to improve productivity such\nas improved education or healthcare will make\nworkforce more efficient and thus reduce per unit\ncosts to better compete with cheaper imports\n(allow more than one supply-side policy)\n• Deregulation policies (e.g. labour laws) to reduce\nproduction costs for firms and therefore they will\nbe able to compete on price with other African\ncountries better\n• Investment in infrastructure to reduce transport\ncosts for exporters\n• Subsidies provided by the government to help\nfirms adjust to new competition, e.g. could be\nused to purchase new, more efficient machinery\n• Demand-side policies such as reduction in taxes\non businesses to reduce their costs and increase\ncompetitiveness on price\n(6)\nPMTPMT",
